 # Daylight master design and agent contract
+
+**D86/D73 coherent turn framework · November 4, 2026.** Owner authorized contextual capture, capture-backed acknowledgments, a shared working assessment of understanding and decision preparation, and deliberate continuation without persona scripts or canned prose. Bind short answers to the actual server-owned displayed question; retain exact answer support, subject/scope, precision, conflict and evidence gates. Composition receives accepted/already-known/unresolved/rejected capture outcomes and existing permissioned reports, learner observations, teaching history and capability holds. Missing records/history never establish that someone did not answer. Tentative conversation progress cannot establish comprehension, external verification or recommendation readiness. Record validation-altered continuation separately from a model-chosen ending; no mandatory follow-up, additional model stage, expanded saved transcript, UI or latency work. Use offline checks only; conversational quality remains owner-assessed. [Implementation and technical evidence](../../audit-evidence/turn-framework-20261104/README.md).
 
 **D86/D90 provider-scoped allowances · November 4, 2026.** Owner requested provider-dependent cost limits after distinguishing local accounting from provider credits. The :8893 allowance is now $5 per UTC day for OpenAI and separately $5 for Anthropic; both GPT models share OpenAI's allowance and retain their exact model prices. Admit below the selected provider's threshold and let the bounded turn/recovery finish, preserving the preceding admission policy. New charge metadata records model/provider atomically; existing charges and holds are retained, with historical attribution only for unique stored pricing/reservation matches. Unknown attribution remains visible and blocks new paid work pending reconciliation; never silently reset or duplicate charges across providers. Preserve the original ledger schema, protected variants' aggregate policies, exact counting/settlement, integrity blocks, privacy and factual gates. Status includes both local provider budgets and explicitly distinguishes them from provider account credits. No UI or conversation-policy change and no paid/live conversation tests. [Implementation and activation](../../audit-evidence/provider-budgets-20261104/README.md).
 
